  "_doc": [
      "Unit conversion table used to produce the US customary J1939 database from the metric (SI) Digital Annex.",
      "Each conversion maps a canonical metric unit to a US unit: us_value = metric_value * scale + offset.",
      "For a parameter with Resolution r and Offset o, the US database stores Resolution r*scale and Offset o*scale + offset.",
      "Aliases are compared after lower-casing and removing spaces, dots, dashes, underscores, '*' and middle dots; the degree sign becomes 'deg'.",
      "US labels follow the conventions of the original CSU-RP1210 database (psi, deg F, mph, miles, gallons, lb, hp).",
      "Remove an entry to keep that unit metric in the US database (for example, delete 'nm' to keep N*m)."
  ],
